# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/

# public/ is generated from art_src/ by `npm run art`, but it is committed
# anyway, because it is what gets deployed.
#
# Building it in CI instead would mean installing Python, Pillow and ffmpeg
# there, and a keying bug would take the site down rather than merely looking
# wrong on somebody's machine. Committing the output costs some binary churn
# whenever art is re-rolled and means the thing deployed is exactly the thing
# that was played.

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local environment overrides
*.local
.env
.env.*

# Python bytecode from the art tooling.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The original audio downloads are kept out of the repository.
#
# public/sfx and public/music are tracked, because they are what the game loads
# and what gets deployed -- audio bundled inside a game is the ordinary use these
# licences are written for. These two directories are the untouched originals as
# they came off Pixabay, which is closer to redistributing the sounds as sounds,
# and the game does not need them to run. Every file is credited by name and id
# in CREDITS.md, so nothing is lost by leaving the originals out.
art_src/sfx/
art_src/music/
